before Nintendo became Nintendo it was a  card company that began in 1889 by  producing traditional Japanese playing  cards one longtime president Hiroshi  Yamauchi took over the family business  in the 1940s he tried to figure out a  way to extend the company's reach he  secured a partnership with the Walt  Disney Company to start creating western  style playing cards with Disney  characters however by the 1960s people  were no longer interested in playing  cards the Japanese gravitated toward  other Hobbies like arcade games and  bowling in a desperate attempt to stay  afloat Nintendo sold everything  literally everything including a toy  vacuum cleaner gunpei yukoi joined  Nintendo in 1965 when the company wasn't  at all involved in video games  he studied electronics at University and  watched his friends get Plum engineering  jobs straight at his school while he  struggled to land a job in his field he  was adamant that he wouldn't need to  leave Kyoto to do it it just so happened  that Nintendo's headquarters were in  Kyoto  Nintendo was never his first choice or  even his second or third choice but out  of desperation he applied not even to  work as an engineer but as a maintenance  staffer  he was hired by Nintendo in 1965. to  maintain the assembly line machines that  manufactured the playing cards he found  he had a lot of time in his hands and  started playing around in the factory  where he had access to the machinery for  his own Amusement he built an extendable  arm toy that could grip things kinda  like this that caught the attention of  President Yamauchi who called yukoi into  his office yukoi thought he was going to  get shoot out by the big boss but  actually the president was impressed by  his inventiveness he asked him to make a  toy that the company could sell at  Christmas according to the book game  over by David Chef ikoi asked his boss  what should I make yamucci replied  something great  he thought he could turn his extended  arm into a great product  the ultra hand was a simple plastic  zigzag contraption that extended and  contracted like an accordion when you  squeeze the handles together it came  with a set of three balls and stands  which could be used for practice the  ultra hand was a great success  Nintendo's first product ever to sell  more than a million units president  Yamauchi then asked hikoi to work on  more toys he designed the ultra machine  which came out in 1967. the ball shot  out to where the player who tried to hit  it it was a good idea to make a toy  related to baseball considering how  popular the sport is in Japan this was  Nintendo's second product to sell over a  million units he koi devised many more  hits including the Love Tester which  supposedly measured the level of  affection between a couple when they  held hands and touched the device it was  the first Nintendo product to run on  electricity though it was quite  rudimentary the love test was yet  another hit but not everything Nintendo  sold was successful one product nearly  killed the company  in 1973 Nintendo came out with a laser  clay so yukoi had the idea of turning  abandoned bowling alleys into shooting  galleries where people fire at clay  pigeons with light beam guns by then  bowling was on the Wane although this  was a clever idea it was expensive and  the timing was terrible the same year  came out OPEC drastically raised the  price of crude oil and gasoline prices  skyrocketed nobody was in the mood to  spend money on toys  Nintendo plunged 5 billion yen in the  red it narrowly escaped but it did and  then became even stronger the bright  side was that laser be paved the way for  the Beloved duck hunt for the classic  shooter video game released a decade  later  with the exception of laser clay many of  Nintendo's early products were a hit  within Japan but didn't reach any level  of global success until the release of  10 billion in 1980. you had to get the  colored balls into the original position  after they were rotated by two drums  this was Nintendo's response to the  Rubik's Cube for many people around the  world yokoi's 10 billion was the first  time they'd heard of Nintendo as the  company grew bigger its research and  development division split into three  units yokoi was in charge of unit 1  which focused on small handheld Games  The Story Goes that yokoi was sitting on  a bullet train one day when he saw a  board businessman fiddling around with  his calculator that's when he realized  the appeal of a portable gain that  anyone could play anywhere at any time  but he had to convince his boss that  this should be the company's Direction  one day when President yamauchi's  chauffeur was off with the flu yokoi  drove the president to a meeting he took  the opportunity to pitch's idea of  creating a portable gaming device but  president Yamauchi didn't seem all that  interested however as fate would have it  yokoi dropped yamayuchi off at a meeting  where he sat beside the president of the  world's largest manufacturer of  calculators sharp and mentioned the idea  to him things took off from there and  Nintendo decided to give portable games  a shot in 1980 Nintendo released Game  and Watch although Game and Watch would  go through 60 different versions what  remained the same was the distinct  cross-shaped control pad this would  later end up on yokoi's Masterpiece the  Game Boy  but I'm getting ahead of myself we're  still a few years away from the Game Boy  things were looking promising for  Nintendo in the early 80s however  starting in 1983 revenues for video game  makers dropped almost 97 in two years  home video game revenues peaked at  around 3.2 billion in 1983 then fell to  100 million by 1985. the industry-wide  decline was blamed on an oversaturated  Market especially in North America where  there were too many consoles to choose  from president Yamauchi also attributed  the crash to poorly designed games he  felt market leader Atari gave too much  power to third-party developers who  produced rubbish games in his words  atari's ET is widely considered the  worst video game of all time  the video game industry also had to fend  off competition from the rise of  personal computers store owners  questioned whether video games were just  a passing fad that would eventually  flame out  then in 1985 Nintendo released the  family computer also known as the  Nintendo Entertainment System  Yamauchi wanted a simple video game  console and that's exactly what  Nintendo's offered it started running as  soon as you turned it on and if there  was a problem all you had to do was  press the reset button to avoid atari's  mistake of poorly designed games  Nintendo strictly controlled third-party  development it introduced a lockout chip  so that any unauthorized games would be  locked out they couldn't be played the  company also decided that approved video  games would carry the official Nintendo  seal Nintendo managed to win back the  Public's trust and the gaming industry  started to recover by 1989 Nintendo  dominated the market earning two and a  half billion in Revenue a year and  around 70 percent of North America's  video game market share largely thanks  to the stunning success of Super Mario  Bros  ikoi would personally Mentor the game's  designer Shigeru Miyamoto ikoi convinced  him to give Mario superhuman qualities  like the ability to fall from any height  unharmed Super Mario Bros helped  Nintendo wipe out its competitors the  mustachioed plumber with overalls and a  red cap was such a hit that Mario became  Nintendo's official mascot  instead of sitting pretty with the  success of the console Nintendo  reinvented itself further when yokoi  invented his greatest success  the bulky gray brick won the hearts of  the world upon its release in 1989. when  nikoi started to design the Game Boy he  implemented a development philosophy  called lateral thinking with withered  technology which means innovative ideas  can lead to new products using  pre-existing technology as opposed to  cutting-edge technology  yokoi's goal was to build a product that  was inexpensive enough to mass produce  so that it was affordable for consumers  and it also had to be fun of course  Nintendo decided to use a monochrome LCD  screen instead of color because the  battery life lasted longer and it was  easier to see under direct sunlight  which allowed people to enjoy playing  Outdoors it wasn't perfect the screen  had a green tint and the characters were  always very blurry yukoi agonized over  that small screen and at one point was  so stressed that he stopped eating and  was diagnosed with acute malnutrition he  recalled I considered it my biggest  failure at one point I honestly  contemplated suicide  yet what he considered his biggest  failure turned out to be his greatest  success what yokoi didn't realize then  was that people are okay with  imperfections kids didn't really care  about the specs they just wanted a fun  highly addictive portable game by the  way the big difference between the Game  Boy and Game and Watch is that Game and  Watch could only play one game  whereas you could swap at the cartridges  on the Game Boy and play whatever game  you wished the Game Boy sold a million  units in the U.S in just a few weeks and  would go on to sell nearly 120 million  units in total worldwide  so when you coil left the company in  1996 to start his own gaming company  people were shocked Japanese Executives  tended to stay at one company for life  some speculated that he was fired also  the follow-up to the Game Boy was a  commercial failure the virtual boy was  costly and uncomfortable to wear  yukoi was 55 years old when he started  kodo laboratory which eventually  released a handheld gaming console  called Wonder swan in partnership with  Bandai in order to compete with the Game  Boy but yokoi would never see Wonder  Swan hit the market because tragedy  struck  [Music]  on October 